[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: learning.SELF-LEARNING
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[SELF_LEARNING]
overview: Agent self-improvement mechanism via documentation updates
purpose: Accumulate project knowledge across sessions
mechanism: When agent discovers rules → update docs → commit → next session reads updated docs

[QUICK_START]
1. During work: Discover a rule or get one from user
2. Check: Is it worth documenting? (see WHEN_TO_UPDATE.toon)
3. Filter: Does it hit the veto list? (see WHEN_NOT_TO_UPDATE.toon)
4. Find: Which file to update (see FILES_REFERENCE.toon)
5. Update: Follow process (see HOW_TO_UPDATE.toon)
6. Verify: Run safety checks (see GUARDRAILS.toon)
7. Commit: Make git commit with [docs] prefix

[DOCUMENTATION_STRUCTURE]
Small modular files in docs/agent/learning/:
  → WHEN_TO_UPDATE.toon        Criteria for documentation updates
  → WHEN_NOT_TO_UPDATE.toon    What NOT to document (veto list)
  → FILES_REFERENCE.toon       Which file for what information
  → HOW_TO_UPDATE.toon         Step-by-step update process
  → EXAMPLES.toon              Concrete update examples
  → GUARDRAILS.toon            Safety checks and filters

[BENEFITS]
- No huge documents to load (read only what needed)
- Modular knowledge (each topic in separate file)
- Easy updates (edit small targeted files)
- Self-documenting (cross-links show structure)
- Knowledge accumulation (each session improves docs)

[NEXT_STEPS]
Start here: → WHEN_TO_UPDATE.toon (understand criteria)
Then: → FILES_REFERENCE.toon (know where to put info)
Finally: → HOW_TO_UPDATE.toon (learn the process)
